    "project": "research/injective_box_audit_20261114/lean",
    "theorem": "InjectiveBoxAudit.injective_box_certificate",
    "statement": "theorem injective_box_certificate : (∀ (T : Type) [Fintype T] [Nonempty T] (A : Finset T), uniformEvent A=(A.card : ℝ)/(Fintype.card T : ℝ) ∧ 0 ≤ uniformEvent A ∧ uniformEvent A ≤ 1) ∧ (∀ (X : Type) [Fintype X] (d : ℕ), Fintype.card (Sample X d)=(Fintype.card X).descFactorial d) ∧ (∀ (X : Type) [Fintype X] (d : ℕ) (h : d ≤ Fintype.card X), (∀ e : Sample X d, (sampleLaw X d h e).toReal=1/((Fintype.card X).descFactorial d : ℝ)) ∧ ∀ B : Fin d → Finset X, boxProbability X d h B=((boxEvent B).card : ℝ)/((Fintype.card X).descFactorial d : ℝ) ∧ boxProbability X d h B ≤ (∏ i, (B i).card : ℕ)/((Fintype.card X).descFactorial d : ℝ)) ∧ (∀ (X : Type) [Fintype X] (d : ℕ), Fintype.card X<d → IsEmpty (PMF (Sample X d))) ∧ (∀ (S : Finset ℤ) (L U : ℝ), L ≤ U → (∀ z ∈ S, L ≤ (z : ℝ) ∧ (z : ℝ) ≤ U) → (S.card : ℝ) ≤ U-L+1) ∧ (∀ (p d : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] (a₀ : ZMod p) (h : d ≤ p-1), Fintype.card (FullSupports p d a₀)=(p-1).descFactorial d ∧ sourceLaw p d a₀ h=@uniformLaw (FullSupports p d a₀) inferInstance (full_support_nonempty a₀ h)) ∧ (∀ (p d : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] (a₀ j : ZMod p), j ≠ 0 → ∀ h : d ≤ p-1, ∀ (L U : Fin d → ℝ), (∀ i, L i ≤ U i) → sourceProbability p d a₀ j h L U ≤ (∏ i, ((p : ℝ)*(U i-L i)+1))/((p-1).descFactorial d : ℝ)) ∧ (∀ (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime], 3 ≤ p → (coordinateBox (0 : ZMod p) 0 0).card=p-1 ∧ ¬ ((coordinateBox (0 : ZMod p) 0 0).card : ℝ) ≤ (p : ℝ)*(0-0)+1) ∧ (∀ (p : ℕ) [Fact p.Prime] (hp : 3 ≤ p) (a₀ : ZMod p), sourceProbability p 1 a₀ 0 (one_dimension_fits hp) (fun _ => 0) (fun _ => 0)=1 ∧ ¬ sourceProbability p 1 a₀ 0 (one_dimension_fits hp) (fun _ => 0) (fun _ => 0) ≤ 1/((p-1 : ℕ) : ℝ))",
    "decl_sha256": "74bd1e4a6ad421bdc085caeacc841339cffa62495e283ed494f6c18499ec6f35",
    "scope": "Exact finite Hildebrand box-counting core for genuine uniform sampling without replacement: actual injective d-tuples have cardinality (card X).descFactorial d, actual point masses and event probability ratios, coordinate-product upper bound without independence assumption, and impossibility of a PMF when d exceeds population. Actual all injective prime-field supports with fixed first point are equivalent to nonzero injective tuples; actual mapped sampler equals uniform law on the full conditional space. Canonical centered coordinates for j nonzero give cardinality at most p*(U-L)+1, so actual source box probability is at most product(width+1)/(p-1).descFactorial d. For all primes p>=3, j=0 gives coordinate cardinality p-1 and actual one-coordinate zero-width source probability 1, directly refuting the deleted-index bound 1/(p-1). Standard foundations/default limits; no holes/custom axioms/native evaluation/raised limits/global flags/waivers/native experiment/paid compute/upload. Corrected asymptotic 1.1 approximation and stronger expected random-support mixing theorem remain open; qualified source theorems not refuted.",
